          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Bloch group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}(\mathbb{C})
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            of the degree-3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homology"} group homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                    %mi grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ♭
                  %mi PSL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3^{grp}(\flat PSL(2,\mathbb{C}), \mathbb{Z})
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+linear+group"} projective linear group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSL(2,\mathbb{C})
            (with
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topological+space"} discrete topology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion subgroup
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z}
          %p
            Accordingly
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                    %mi grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ♭
                  %mi PSL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3^{grp}(\flat PSL(2,\mathbb{C}), \mathbb{Z})
            itself is also called the
            %em extended Bloch group
            (
            %a{:href => "#Neumann04"}> Neumann 04
            ).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToHyperbolic3Manifolds Relation to hyperbolic 3-manifolds
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+class"} fundamental class
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+3-manifold"} hyperbolic 3-manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            canonically gives an element in the Bloch group: let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ℍ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \mathbb{H}^3/\Gamma
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PSL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma\hookrightarrow PSL(2,\mathbb{C})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is that of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\Gamma
            and hence the fundamental class maps forward under
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                    %mi grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                    %mi grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ♭
                  %mi PSL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                    %mi grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ♭
                  %mi PSL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_3(X,\mathbb{Z})
                  \\simeq
                  H_3(B \Gamma, \mathbb{Z})
                  \\simeq
                  H_3^{grp}(\Gamma, \mathbb{Z})
                  \\longrightarrow
                  H_3^{grp}(\flat PSL(2,\mathbb{C}), \mathbb{Z})
                  \\longrightarrow
                  H_3^{grp}(\flat PSL(2,\mathbb{C}), \mathbb{Z})/(\mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z})
                  \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Neumann11"} Neumann 11, section 2.2
          %h3#RelationToCheegerSimonsClass Cheeger-Simons class and complex volume
          %p
            There is a group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ♭
                  %mi PSL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mn 2
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\hat c
                  \\colon
                  H_3(\flat PSL(2,\mathbb{C}), \mathbb{Z})
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbb{C}/\pi^2 \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            such that when applied to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+class"} fundamental class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X]
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+3-manifold"} hyperbolic 3-manifold
            according to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#RelationToHyperbolic3Manifolds"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+volume"} complex volume
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi cs
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi i
                  %mi vol
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\hat c([X]) = cs(X) + i vol(X)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cheeger-Simons+class"} Cheeger-Simons class
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Neumann11"} Neumann 11, section 2.3
          %h3#RelationToAlgebraicKTheory Relation to algebraic K-theory
          %p
            Up to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroups"} torsion subgroups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi K
                    %mn 3
                    %mi ind
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_3^{ind}(\mathbb{C})
            (
            %a{:href => "#Suslin90"}> Suslin90
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Zickert09"} Zickert 09
          %h3#RelationToTheBorelRegulator Relation to the Borel regulator
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+number+field"} algebraic number field
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi k
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\sigma_i \colon k \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C}\}
            its complex embeddings, write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi vol
                    %mi i
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi vol
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi PSL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  vol_i \coloneqq vol \circ (\sigma_i)_\ast \colon
                  H_3(PSL(2,k),\mathbb{Z})
                  \\to
                  \\mathbb{R}
          %p
            for the induced volume measures, using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cheeger-Simons+class"} Cheeger-Simons class
            from
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#RelationToCheegerSimonsClass"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product"} direct product
            of these volumes is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+regulator"} Borel regulator
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Borel
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi vol
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi vol
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi PSL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Borel \coloneqq (vol_1, \cdots, vol_{r_2})
                  \\colon
                  H_3(PSL(2,\mathbb{C}), \mathbb{Z})
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbb{R}^{r_2}
                  \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Zickert09"} Zickert 09, (1.2)
          %p
            Now the point is that restricted to the Bloch group proper the Borel regulator is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective"} injective
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Neumann11"} Neumann 11, theorem 2.4
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+manifold"} hyperbolic manifold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cheeger-Simons+class"}> Cheeger-Simons class
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+volume"} complex volume
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+regulator"} Borel regulator
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Neumann04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Neumann"}> Walter Neumann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Extended Bloch group and the Cheeger-Chern-Simons class
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0307092"} arXiv:math/0307092
          %p
            The relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+regulator"} Borel regulator
            is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Chih-Han Sah,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homology of classical Lie groups made discrete. III.
            %li#Suslin90
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Suslin"}> Andrei Suslin
                \.
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi K
                            %mn 3
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_3
                    of a field, and the Bloch group
            %li#Zickert09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Zickert"}> Christian Zickert
                ,
                %em The extended Bloch group and algebraic K-theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.4005"}> arXiv:0910.4005
                )
          %p Review is in
          %ul
            %li#Neumann11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Neumann"}> Walter Neumann
              , section 2.4
              = succeed "," do
                %em Realizing arithmetic invariants of hyperbolic 3-manifolds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1108.0062"} arXiv:1108.0062
